###############################################################################
# Line endings.
#
# Files here are bind-mounted straight from the working tree into Linux
# containers, so a Windows checkout must not turn them into CRLF:
#
#   scripts/*.sh          -> ./scripts:/init in the db-init service. With CRLF,
#                            "set -euo pipefail" itself fails ("invalid option
#                            name"), so none of -e/-u/-o take effect, every psql
#                            call fails unnoticed, and the script still exits 0 —
#                            compose reads that as service_completed_successfully
#                            and starts the services against databases that were
#                            never created.
#   *.yaml/*.yml, .env    -> dapr components, mediamtx.yml, compose env files.
#
# .ps1/.cmd go the other way: Windows is the only thing that runs them.
###############################################################################
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
.env        text eol=lf
.env.*      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
